course: dictionary
lesson: 11889
title: Brief: short and to the point
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brief means short. It can describe time or length: «The rain was only a brief shower.» A shower that is brief does not last long, so brief must mean short.
explain: Brief can also mean using few words. «Please be brief, because we only have one minute.» The teacher wants you to get to the point quickly, without a long talk. A brief summary is a short version of a story that keeps only the main points.
explain: Brief can also be a set of instructions for a job. «The design brief tells us to build a bridge from paper.» A brief gives you the facts you need to do the task. When someone briefs you, they tell you what you need to know.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in short. «A brief visit» becomes «a short visit», and the sentence still makes sense. That is a good sign that brief means short here.
fact: Brief means short in time or length, or using few words.
fact: «Briefly explain» means explain in a few words.
fact: A brief is a set of instructions about a task, such as a design brief.
fact: To brief someone is to give them the facts or instructions they need.
fact: «In brief» means in a few words, as a short version.
exercise: «The rain was only a brief shower.» What does brief mean here? | Heavy and long | Cold and windy | *Short | Hidden
exercise: «Please be brief, we only have one minute.» What does brief mean here? | Full of jokes | *Using few words | Very loud | Slowly and carefully
exercise: «The design brief tells us what to make.» What is a brief in this sentence? | A kind of bridge | *Instructions about a job | A short nap | A pencil case
test: «Mum gave me a brief summary of the story.» Find and copy the word that means short. | *brief | Mum | story | summary
test: To brief someone means to | Run very fast | Tell them a joke | Hide them from the sun | *Give them the facts or instructions they need
exam: «Tell me the story in brief.» What does «in brief» mean? | In the morning | In a loud voice | *In a few words | In a very long way
